        "test": "BitShiftOpTest.RightShiftByMoreThanBitWidth_Uint64",
        "notes": "Diverges from the upstream test's inputs (inputs.x shape [2] values [1000, 42] -> shape [3] values [1000, 42, 1000]; inputs.y shape [2] values [33, 64] -> shape [3] values [33, 64, 3]); the expected output is recomputed by the CPU reference for the new inputs. Projects the uint64 source case to supported uint32 storage while preserving shift-past-width semantics, with a trailing in-range shift as the control that a kernel zeroing every shift would fail."
